:: Patchnotes
<<nobr>>
		/* These are patchnotes.
		   Organized by new content - QoL adjustments - patched bugs - new bugs.
		   Should have a current focus tab somewhere...
		   The gleeful tone is neecessary for personal success. */

	<h1> Pre-Pre-Alpha 0.31.3.8</h1>
	<em><strong>COLONIST UPDATE</strong></em>
	
	<ul>
	<li>Colonist IDs! You won't see these, but under the hood, this is how the game keeps track of unique individuals for things like, say... relationships! So if you have multiple dragons named 'Sparky' or what have you, the game won't try to call every Sparky that ever existed.</li>
	<li>Colonists have once again been modified by A Lot. Eggs and hatchlings now store complete data of what they'll be when they're grown, and parents, since...</li>
	<li>Colonists can have eggs together! Parents are tracked, though nothing else is. This is the start of a relationship system. To accompany this, there's a new social policy tracking if colonists are allowed to breed, otherwise things get ridiculous REAL quick. This will be tinkered with regularly.</li>
	<li>Job icons! Thunder list has icons next to titles for at-a-glance recognition.</li>
	<li>New job! <strong>Salvagers</strong> look for gold for you! Since their job is specifically to get gold, while they don't often find any, they bring in a <em>lot</em> when they do. Maybe.</li>
	<li>The start of job sites! Currently not constructable, plans are in place. Will provide buffs based on upgrade level, similar to the moat structure.</li>
	<li>Personalities have been restructured into archetypes; previous personalities are now defined as 'traits'. Certain archetypes are good at certain jobs, and prefer (or disdain) the company of other archetypes... except for lazy personalities, who don't want to do work and don't like anyone but other lazy dragons. No one much cares for lazy dragons either. Interact page has been updated to reflect archetypes, though information on what archetypes like who / what jobs is not yet available. Will be soon, prommie.</li>
	<li>Encylopedia real?! Encyclopedia real! Presently, there is only a tutorial refresher, as well as some loose explanations of dragon personalities. Details will be added per dev fiat, and whenever I manage to revive my laptop / get the data out of it. =)</li>
	<li>Player's den operates as a trophy room. Perhaps trophies will later have a purpose...?</li>
	<li></li>
	</ul><br>

	<strong>QoL</strong>
	<ul>
	<li>Minor accessibility improvements, hopefully. Links are now underlined, and images have alt-text. Images currently limited to dragon-list icons, but that may change.</li>
	<li>Re-organized Dragon List in thunder management; should be much more functional now. Includes quick-access to assigning dragons jobs.</li>
	<li>Self-assign shelters and auto-load rockfalls are checks now, since there was some confusion with the previous selection method.</li>
	<li>Foraging end-of has been moved to its own page. It checks what isn't topped in your stores before presenting options, and if you're full-up on everything (including having looked for gold), just tells you to go home.</li>
	<li>The above also applies to the Central foraging options: It will no longer present foraging options if all of your stores are full, and you've looked for valuables.</li>
	<li>The buildQueue can have items removed via clicking on them in the Building page. Yay! Now those millions of hollows can be removed from your queue. =)</li>
	<li>In a QoL for me, not for thee: `endDay` has been seperated into multiple widgets, with `endDay` itself operating as a master widget. Makes things a touch more organized in the backend, and has allowed me to comment on it THOROUGHLY.</li>
	<li></li>
	</ul><br>

	<strong>Balancing</strong>
	<ul>
	<li>Clamped how much a single resource-gatherer can bring in; one forager should no longer feed a colony of thirty-six with no support from the founder. They are currently capped at a minimum of 1, and a maximum of 35 for all general resources. This does not affect the total, only individuals. One forager could haul 35 food in a day at most; a second brings back 10. They still bring 45 food in total. Soldiers can bring back more when they hunt, due to specifically hunting large game, and salvagers are capped by skill. They do what they like.</li>
	<li>To further this: if a dragon's personality aligns with their job, the cap is higher, but still capped! Just because a dreamy dragon is foraging, they can't get 100 food! They'll just pick up a max of 45 instead, with higher chances to collect more. (job preferences and personalities will continue to be refined.)</li>
	<li>Not sheltering dragons is now more punishing. Put them in a rut or a hollow, but DO NOT let them out in the cold.</li>
	<li>The player also consumes SLIGHTLY more on a daily basis if sheltered. Only one more—4 food, 5 water—to better reflect the change to the rest of their grown colonists.</li>
	<li>goldBonus has once again been nerfed. I'll figure it out.</li>
	<li>Bit more of a grace period before the Hydra raid starts; players somewhat more time to put up defenses & make sure their dragons are ready to go.</li>
	<li>"What's the harm in Salvagers having no cap? Their chances of bringing in gold is slim," thought I. Then I bore horrified witness to three salvagers apparently pillaging a settlement for 1177 gold in one evening. Salvagers capped; those who like their job can bring in up to 75 (with a SLIGHTLY higher chance of succeeding their checks), those who don't can bring in up to 50 (with a slightly lower chance of succeeding in finding gold at all), or they might have bad luck and find nothing at all. Dragons still <em>really</em> like gold, after all.</li>
	<li></li>
	</ul><br>

	<strong>Bugs Patched</strong>
	<ul>
	<li>Double 'ands' should no longer occur during day end when dragons interact with the housing system.</li>
	<li>Dragons in returnee event should no longer say they left because 'wanderer', 'colony' or other similar mix-ups.</li>
	<li>Encountering the Hydra Den post-victory directs the PC to the visit page now.</li>
	<li>Builders should no longer report 0 days left until a building is finished; they should just finish the building. Oughta help a touch with defense preparations.</li>
	<li>Central no longer allows foraging if your stores are capped... not sure how I missed that, to be quite honest.</li>
	<li>Builders now actually build things instead of constantly 'starting work'. Again.</li>
	<li>Dragons no longer breed with eggs / hatchlings. They also stop the egg factory when there's no more room in the nursery, rather than making the nests overfloweth.</li>
	<li>It was pointed out to me that the order of the resources on the side v. how they're presented when choosing what to forage for differ. That can't stand.</li>
	<li>Everydragon is counted properly. Remember to always double-check your writing when you've been doing something for several hours or else you'll miss something silly and obvious. <3 </li>
	<li>No longer able to preview eggs/hatchlings via the Interact page. That was fun while it lasted.</li>
	<li>Dragons should accurately report how many days they've worked / how good they are at their jobs in the Interact page.</li>
	<li>It's clearer that Scavengers are bringing in the 'they also found (whatever) gold!' rather than your salvs.</li>
	<li>Moat construction slightly reworded to imply that it's a multi-step process.</li>
	<li>Thunder page works again; sad as we are to see Undefined go, it's for the best.</li>
	<li>Dragons stop saying they suck at their job when they're actually veterans in the Interact page. (I broke a lot of things in the Interact page.)</li>
	<li>When choosing to take in every wanderer / more than one wanderer, they should actually appropriately join rather than deciding their planet needs them.</li>
	<li>Wanderers once again have xp for jobs. weird bug, that one.</li>
	<li></li>
	</ul><br>
	
	<strong>Bugs Created</strong>
	<ul>
	<li>'Cheating' link in Bugtesting/Cheating mode doesn't have an underline. Bit of a headscratcher, that.</li>
	<li>I've probably made bugs in relation to the colonist refactor. Sorry.</li>
	<li>Hatchling & Egg 'first grown/hatched' events not firing. I'm really not sure what's going on there, but I'll get it. Until then, a bit of flavor is missing.</li>
	<li>The breeding system does not care about parentage. I'm going to figure that out, to try and minimize line-breeding.</li>
	<li></li>
	</ul><br>

	<sup>Hey, if you're reading this? The dev loves you <3 </sup>
<</nobr>>

:: OOC Chat
<<nobr>>

		/* This is the 'end demo' page.
		   Any time I reach a new milestone in DREKI, this page will be updated to congratulate the player on reaching the current 'end'.
		   It includes hints on if the player has missed anything or if they've found it all, and a teaser on what's the next 'big' update.
		   This page always returns to either the Sandbox, or to the game START.
	
		   CURRENT DEMO END: Hydra Raid. */

	Hello, this is the dev here! I've some words to share...<br><br>

	First, thank you for playing DREKI—and for playing it so long that you've reached the end of the current 'story' content.
	<<if $hydraBeat == true>>
		<<if $player.specials[0] == "Hydra">>
			A truly well-deserved congratulations on achieving the special raid ending, too; that's no easy feat! I hope you've enjoyed. Though there's no more major / pseudo-story content to be found, you can continue to play in your current colony for as long as you like.<br><br>
		<<else>>
			You've beaten the big boss of the current content, and a hearty congratulations is in order! That's no mean feat... though there's something extra you've missed. Maybe if you had stronger defenses, you'd find something more? but that's neither here nor there. Congratulations no less, and a hearty <em>well done!</em> You're free to continue playing this colony to your heart's content, or you can try again with that raid and maybe get the special ending. Good luck!<br><br>
		<</if>>

		DREKI is still in active development, and more will be coming. This is merely a teaser!... and a fairly incomplete one at that. If you have encountered any bugs, confusion, or difficulties, please report it! You can do so at the <a href="https://github.com/DrekiWork/DREKI/issues">GitHub page</a>, or on <a href="https://drekidev.itch.io/dreki">itch.io</a>. Feel free to swing on by even if you didn't—maybe if you've got some thoughts you'd like to share, or suggestions you might like to see. I'm all ears!<br><br>
		
		Otherwise, I intend to do housekeeping for a while, before focusing on matters closer to home... Specifically, colonists!<br><br>

		Once more, from the bottom of my heart—thank you for playing. May the wind stay under your wings, and I hope you continue to enjoy DREKI.<br><br>

		[[Now, back to the game.|Sandbox Central]]

	<<else>>

		The hydra is intended to be a tough fight; there's no shame in losing here. You can always try again! Either way, I hope you've enjoyed what you've played so far.<br><br>

		DREKI is still in active development, and more will be coming. This is merely a teaser!... and a fairly incomplete one at that. If you have encountered any bugs, confusion, or difficulties, please report it! You can do so at the <a href="https://github.com/DrekiWork/DREKI/issues">GitHub page</a>, or on <a href="https://drekidev.itch.io/dreki">itch.io</a>. Feel free to swing on by even if you didn't—maybe if you've got some thoughts you'd like to share, or suggestions you might like to see. I'm all ears!<br><br>
		
		Otherwise, I intend to do housekeeping for a while, before focusing on matters closer to home... Specifically, colonists!<br><br>

		Once more, from the bottom of my heart—thank you for playing. May the wind stay under your wings, and I hope you continue to enjoy DREKI.<br><br>

		[[Now, back to the game.|START]]

	<</if>>
<</nobr>>